IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `maca-core`
IMPORT `maca-seat`

-- Motor Accidents (Compensation) Act 1979 (NT) -- cases for the injured person's seat (maca-seat.l4) and the regulative rules of
-- the core (maca-core.l4).
--
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text (REPM022 of the Act, REPM022R1 of the Regulations), with the
-- arithmetic in the comment above the assertion. Figures the deposit does not give (average weekly earnings, MA, CPI) are round
-- illustrative inputs, not the published figures.
--
-- A breached or still-pending DEONTIC cannot be asserted on the stable l4, so regulative rules are asserted where the trace ends
-- FULFILLED, and #TRACEd with an "-- expect:" line where it does not. Clock: days.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the injured person`

GIVEN `d` IS A NUMBER
      `m` IS A NUMBER
      `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`on` `d` `m` `y` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY `d` `m` `y`

§§ `Helpers: the seat's questions asked with a list of the facts that are true`

-- Am I entitled (s 7)? The facts that are true are named in `flags`.
GIVEN `flags` IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH AN `Entitlement answer`
`coverage with` `flags` MEANS
    `Am I entitled to motor accident benefits` (`has` "self-propelled") (`has` "rails") (`has` "slow wheelchair") (`has` "200 W cycle") (`has` "driven") (`has` "out of control") (`has` "collision") (`has` "hurt in it") (`has` "hurt helping") (`has` "in the Territory") (`has` "in Australia") (`has` "Territory vehicle") (`has` "3 months") (`has` "not living in the Territory") (`has` "outside 6 months") (`has` "main home or job outside") (`has` "left for good") (`has` "claimed elsewhere")
    WHERE
        GIVEN `f` IS A STRING
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        `has` `f` MEANS elem `f` `flags`

-- A car driven in the Territory, the person hurt in it: the base case for coverage.
`a Territory crash` MEANS LIST "self-propelled", "driven", "hurt in it", "in the Territory", "in Australia", "Territory vehicle", "3 months"

-- Which benefits does Part 3 exclude? The breath reading is given; the facts that are true are named in `flags`.
GIVEN `day`    IS A DATE
      `breath` IS A NUMBER
      `flags`  IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Part 3 exclusion`
`Part 3 on` `day` `at breath` `breath` `with` `flags` MEANS
    `Which of my benefits are excluded` `day` (`has` "driving") (`has` "over the limit") `breath` 0 (`has` "refused sample") (`has` "excuse") (`has` "Commission: alcohol contributed") (`has` "shown not to contribute") (`has` "conduct contributed") (`has` "found guilty") (`has` "reckless") (`has` "never licensed") (`has` "suspended") (`has` "cancelled") (`has` "expired 3 months") (`has` "licence conditions") (`has` "emergency") (`has` "in a vehicle") (`has` "owner") (`has` "unregistered 3 months") (`has` "unregistrable") (`has` "knew unregistered") (`has` "conditionally registered") (`has` "knew conditional") (`has` "breach of registration conditions") (`has` "other registered vehicle") (`has` "stole") (`has` "indictable offence") (`has` "escape") (`has` "intent to injure") (`has` "workers compensation") (`has` "motor sport") (`has` "in the event") (`has` "terrorist")
    WHERE
        GIVEN `f` IS A STRING
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        `has` `f` MEANS elem `f` `flags`

`10 March 2025` MEANS `on` 10 3 2025

-- The weekly benefit (ss 13, 14, 33). Dates and amounts are given; the facts that are true are named in `flags` ("s 33": the
-- Commission extended the s 13(5)(a) limit, to the day `extended`).
GIVEN `accident` IS A DATE
      `week`     IS A DATE
      `born`     IS A DATE
      `pension`  IS A DATE
      `MA`       IS A NUMBER
      `calc`     IS A NUMBER
      `earned`   IS A NUMBER
      `other`    IS A NUMBER
      `stopped`  IS A DATE
      `extended` IS A DATE
      `flags`    IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A `Weekly benefit answer`
`weekly` `accident` `week` `born` `pension` `MA` `calc` `earned` `other` `stopped` `extended` `flags` MEANS
    `How much weekly compensation do I get this week` `accident` `week` `born` `pension` (`has` "s 33") `extended` (`has` "reduced") (`has` "earning on accident day") `MA` (`has` "full time") `earned` `calc` (`has` "prison") (`has` "outside Australia") (`has` "student") (`has` "married at accident") (`has` "low earnings") (`has` "stopped study") `stopped` (`has` "married or dependant") (`has` "no seatbelt") `other`
    WHERE
        GIVEN `f` IS A STRING
        GIVETH A BOOLEAN
        `has` `f` MEANS elem `f` `flags`

-- A 39-year-old (born 1 June 1985; pension age 67 on 1 June 2052) hurt on 10 March 2025; MA $1,500; the Commission's s 13(3)
-- figure $1,200; the week from Monday 17 March 2025.
`born 1985` MEANS `on` 1 6 1985
`pension 2052` MEANS `on` 1 6 2052
`17 March 2025` MEANS `on` 17 3 2025
`any day` MEANS `on` 1 1 2000

§§ `ss 4, 4A, 4B, 7 -- coverage`

-- s 7(1): a motor accident in the Territory.
#ASSERT `coverage with` `a Territory crash` EQUALS `entitled: a motor accident in the Territory (s 7(1))`
-- s 4 "motor vehicle" does not include "(a) a vehicle that runs on rails": a tram is not one, so there is no motor accident.
#ASSERT `coverage with` (LIST "self-propelled", "rails", "driven", "hurt in it", "in the Territory", "in Australia", "3 months") EQUALS `not entitled: it was not a motor accident (s 4A)`
-- s 4 (c): "a cycle powered by an engine with a power output not exceeding 200 watts" is not a motor vehicle.
#ASSERT `coverage with` (LIST "self-propelled", "200 W cycle", "out of control", "hurt in it", "in the Territory", "in Australia", "3 months") EQUALS `not entitled: it was not a motor accident (s 4A)`
-- s 4A(2): the occurrence must result directly from driving, loss of control or a collision; an injury from none of them is not one.
#ASSERT `coverage with` (LIST "self-propelled", "hurt in it", "in the Territory", "in Australia", "3 months") EQUALS `not entitled: it was not a motor accident (s 4A)`
-- s 4A(3): a person hurt helping at the scene.
#ASSERT `coverage with` (LIST "self-propelled", "collision", "hurt helping", "in the Territory", "in Australia") EQUALS `entitled: a motor accident in the Territory (s 7(1))`
-- s 7(1) asks nothing about residence: a visitor hurt in the Territory is covered.
#ASSERT `coverage with` (LIST "self-propelled", "driven", "hurt in it", "in the Territory", "in Australia", "not living in the Territory", "main home or job outside") EQUALS `entitled: a motor accident in the Territory (s 7(1))`
-- s 7(2): a Territory resident hurt in Queensland by a Territory-registered car.
#ASSERT `coverage with` (LIST "self-propelled", "driven", "hurt in it", "in Australia", "Territory vehicle", "3 months") EQUALS `entitled: a Territory resident, in a motor accident elsewhere in Australia arising out of the use of a Territory motor vehicle (s 7(2))`
-- s 7(2)(b): the same, but the car was registered in Queensland.
#ASSERT `coverage with` (LIST "self-propelled", "driven", "hurt in it", "in Australia", "3 months") EQUALS `not entitled: the accident happened outside the Territory and did not arise out of the use of a Territory motor vehicle (s 7(2)(b))`
-- s 7(2)(a): a Territory car in Bali.
#ASSERT `coverage with` (LIST "self-propelled", "driven", "hurt in it", "Territory vehicle", "3 months") EQUALS `not entitled: the accident happened outside Australia (s 7(2)(a))`
-- ss 4B(1), 7(2): two months in the Territory is not "at least 3 months".
#ASSERT `coverage with` (LIST "self-propelled", "driven", "hurt in it", "in Australia", "Territory vehicle") EQUALS `not entitled: the accident happened outside the Territory and the person was not a resident of the Territory (ss 4B, 7(2))`
-- s 7(3)(b): having claimed damages in Queensland, "the claimant's entitlement to statutory benefits ceases".
#ASSERT `coverage with` (LIST "self-propelled", "driven", "hurt in it", "in Australia", "Territory vehicle", "3 months", "claimed elsewhere") EQUALS `no longer entitled: a claim for damages or compensation was made in the place of the accident (s 7(3)(b))`
-- s 7(3) is for a person entitled "under subsection (2)": a claim elsewhere does not end an s 7(1) entitlement.
#ASSERT `coverage with` (LIST "self-propelled", "driven", "hurt in it", "in the Territory", "in Australia", "3 months", "claimed elsewhere") EQUALS `entitled: a motor accident in the Territory (s 7(1))`

-- s 4B. (1) three months; (2)(a) not living in the Territory and 6 months away, or main home or job elsewhere; (2)(b) left for good.
#ASSERT `Was I a Territory resident at my accident` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`Was I a Territory resident at my accident` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Was I a Territory resident at my accident` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`Was I a Territory resident at my accident` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE))
-- Away for 2 months on a trip, home and job still in the Territory: still a resident.
#ASSERT `Was I a Territory resident at my accident` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
-- (2)(b) applies even while still living in the Territory.
#ASSERT (NOT (`Was I a Territory resident at my accident` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE))

§§ `Part 3 -- exclusions (ss 9-10C, 11B; regs 4A, 4B)`

-- Reg 4A(1): "0.08 grams or more per 210 litres": 0.08 is enough, 0.079 is not; (b) the blood reading; (5), (6) a refusal.
#ASSERT `Must alcohol be presumed to have contributed to my accident` 0.08 0 FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`Must alcohol be presumed to have contributed to my accident` 0.079 0 FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `Must alcohol be presumed to have contributed to my accident` 0 0.1 FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Must alcohol be presumed to have contributed to my accident` 0 0 TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT (NOT (`Must alcohol be presumed to have contributed to my accident` 0 0 TRUE TRUE))

#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0 `with` EMPTY EQUALS `no exclusion applies`
-- s 9: driving over the limit with a breath reading of 0.12; s 9(2) presumes the alcohol contributed. s 9(3): loss of earning capacity
-- and the impairment lump sum.
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0.12 `with` (LIST "driving", "over the limit") EQUALS `no compensation for loss of earning capacity and no lump sum for permanent impairment` (LIST "s 9")
-- s 9(2) "unless the contrary is established": shown that the alcohol did not contribute.
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0.12 `with` (LIST "driving", "over the limit", "shown not to contribute") EQUALS `no exclusion applies`
-- A drug, with no presumption: the Commission's opinion that it contributed (s 9(1)(c)).
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0 `with` (LIST "driving", "over the limit", "Commission: alcohol contributed") EQUALS `no compensation for loss of earning capacity and no lump sum for permanent impairment` (LIST "s 9")
-- s 9 is for the driver: a passenger over the limit is not excluded.
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0.12 `with` (LIST "over the limit", "in a vehicle") EQUALS `no exclusion applies`
-- s 9A: conduct that contributed and a conviction for dangerous driving.
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0 `with` (LIST "driving", "conduct contributed", "found guilty") EQUALS `no compensation for loss of earning capacity and no lump sum for permanent impairment` (LIST "s 9A")
-- s 9A needs the conviction as well as the Commission's opinion.
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0 `with` (LIST "driving", "conduct contributed") EQUALS `no exclusion applies`
-- s 9B: recklessly ignoring a substantial risk (surfing on a car roof).
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0 `with` (LIST "reckless") EQUALS `no compensation for loss of earning capacity and no lump sum for permanent impairment` (LIST "s 9B")
-- s 9C(1)(b)(i): a driver who never held a licence; (2) not in an emergency.
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0 `with` (LIST "driving", "never licensed") EQUALS `no compensation for loss of earning capacity and no lump sum for permanent impairment` (LIST "s 9C")
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0 `with` (LIST "driving", "never licensed", "emergency") EQUALS `no exclusion applies`
-- s 9C(1)(b)(iv): a licence expired 3 months or more; a licence suspended only for unpaid fines is not caught (the input says so).
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0 `with` (LIST "driving", "expired 3 months") EQUALS `no compensation for loss of earning capacity and no lump sum for permanent impairment` (LIST "s 9C")
-- s 9D: an owner-driver who knew the car had been unregistered for 3 months, hit by a registered car being driven: all benefits but
-- ss 18, 18BC, 18BD and 19 (s 9D(3)).
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0 `with` (LIST "driving", "in a vehicle", "owner", "unregistered 3 months", "knew unregistered", "other registered vehicle") EQUALS `only medical and rehabilitation, long-term and interim attendant care and appliance benefits are payable` (LIST "s 9D")
-- Finding 8: the owner as a passenger, who did not know, is excluded all the same: s 9D(1)(d) asks knowledge of the driver only.
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0 `with` (LIST "in a vehicle", "owner", "unregistered 3 months", "other registered vehicle") EQUALS `only medical and rehabilitation, long-term and interim attendant care and appliance benefits are payable` (LIST "s 9D")
-- ... while the owner who drove it, not knowing and with no reason to know, is not excluded.
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0 `with` (LIST "driving", "in a vehicle", "owner", "unregistered 3 months", "other registered vehicle") EQUALS `no exclusion applies`
-- s 9D(1)(d)(i): a reg 4B vehicle that cannot be registered needs no knowledge.
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0 `with` (LIST "driving", "in a vehicle", "unregistered 3 months", "unregistrable", "other registered vehicle") EQUALS `only medical and rehabilitation, long-term and interim attendant care and appliance benefits are payable` (LIST "s 9D")
-- s 9E: the same owner-driver, but alone on the road: "No benefits are payable".
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0 `with` (LIST "driving", "in a vehicle", "owner", "unregistered 3 months", "knew unregistered") EQUALS `no benefits are payable at all` (LIST "s 9E")
-- s 9E(2): an emergency.
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0 `with` (LIST "driving", "in a vehicle", "owner", "unregistered 3 months", "knew unregistered", "emergency") EQUALS `no exclusion applies`
-- s 9F: a conditionally registered vehicle driven in breach of its conditions, with another lawful vehicle involved.
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0 `with` (LIST "driving", "in a vehicle", "owner", "conditionally registered", "breach of registration conditions", "other registered vehicle") EQUALS `only medical and rehabilitation, long-term and interim attendant care and appliance benefits are payable` (LIST "s 9F")
-- s 9G: the same alone.
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0 `with` (LIST "driving", "in a vehicle", "owner", "conditionally registered", "breach of registration conditions") EQUALS `no benefits are payable at all` (LIST "s 9G")
-- s 9F(1)(c)(ii): a driver who is not the owner and did not know of the conditions is outside ss 9F and 9G.
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0 `with` (LIST "driving", "in a vehicle", "conditionally registered", "breach of registration conditions") EQUALS `no exclusion applies`
-- s 10(a): criminally responsible for the theft of a vehicle involved.
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0 `with` (LIST "driving", "in a vehicle", "stole") EQUALS `no benefits are payable at all` (LIST "s 10")
-- s 10A: compensable under the Return to Work Act 1986.
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0 `with` (LIST "in a vehicle", "workers compensation") EQUALS `no benefits are payable at all` (LIST "s 10A")
-- s 10B: a passenger in a car in an informal drag race.
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0 `with` (LIST "in a vehicle", "motor sport", "in the event") EQUALS `no benefits are payable at all` (LIST "s 10B")
-- s 10B(1): a bystander with no link to the event is not caught.
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0 `with` (LIST "motor sport") EQUALS `no exclusion applies`
-- s 10C: a terrorist act.
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0 `with` (LIST "terrorist") EQUALS `no benefits are payable at all` (LIST "s 10C")
-- s 11B, cumulative: a drunk, unlicensed owner-driver of a car unregistered for 3 months, hit by a registered car. The widest (s 9D)
-- governs and all three are listed.
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0.15 `with` (LIST "driving", "over the limit", "never licensed", "in a vehicle", "owner", "unregistered 3 months", "knew unregistered", "other registered vehicle") EQUALS `only medical and rehabilitation, long-term and interim attendant care and appliance benefits are payable` (LIST "s 9", "s 9C", "s 9D")
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` `10 March 2025` `at breath` 0.15 `with` (LIST "driving", "over the limit", "in a vehicle", "stole") EQUALS `no benefits are payable at all` (LIST "s 9", "s 10")
-- s 46: Part 3 as amended in 2014 applies to accidents after 1 July 2014 commenced; the day before is outside this encoding.
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` (`on` 30 6 2014) `at breath` 0 `with` EMPTY EQUALS `outside this encoding: the accident happened before 1 July 2014, and Part 3 as it stood before the 2014 amendments is not deposited (s 46)`
#ASSERT `Part 3 on` (`on` 1 7 2014) `at breath` 0 `with` EMPTY EQUALS `no exclusion applies`

-- s 11(1)(b): "of or above the age of 16 years". Born 11 March 2008: 15 on 10 March 2024, 16 on 11 March 2024.
#ASSERT `Are my benefits reduced for no seatbelt or helmet` (`on` 11 3 2008) (`on` 10 3 2024) TRUE EQUALS `not reduced under s 11`
#ASSERT `Are my benefits reduced for no seatbelt or helmet` (`on` 11 3 2008) (`on` 11 3 2024) TRUE EQUALS `reduced by 25% under s 11`
#ASSERT `Are my benefits reduced for no seatbelt or helmet` `born 1985` `10 March 2025` FALSE EQUALS `not reduced under s 11`
-- Finding 24: s 11 was substituted in 2014 (endnotes: "sub No. 20, 2014, s 8") and s 46(2) keeps the earlier Part 3 for an earlier
-- accident. An unbelted adult hurt on 1 May 2013, or on 30 June 2014: outside this encoding. On 1 July 2014: reduced.
#ASSERT `Are my benefits reduced for no seatbelt or helmet` `born 1985` (`on` 1 5 2013) TRUE EQUALS `outside this encoding: the accident happened before 1 July 2014, and s 11 as it stood before the 2014 amendments is not deposited (s 46)`
#ASSERT `Are my benefits reduced for no seatbelt or helmet` `born 1985` (`on` 30 6 2014) TRUE EQUALS `outside this encoding: the accident happened before 1 July 2014, and s 11 as it stood before the 2014 amendments is not deposited (s 46)`
#ASSERT `Are my benefits reduced for no seatbelt or helmet` `born 1985` (`on` 1 7 2014) TRUE EQUALS `reduced by 25% under s 11`

§§ `ss 13(5)(a), 33 -- when weekly compensation stops`

-- (i): an accident more than 2 years before pension age: it stops at pension age.
#ASSERT `When does my weekly compensation stop` `10 March 2025` `pension 2052` FALSE `any day` EQUALS `pension 2052`
-- (ii): pension age exactly 2 years after the accident is not "more than 2 years": 104 weeks (728 days) after the accident.
-- 10 March 2025 to 10 March 2027 is 730 days (no 29 February between), so 728 days is 8 March 2027.
#ASSERT `When does my weekly compensation stop` `10 March 2025` (`on` 10 3 2027) FALSE `any day` EQUALS `on` 8 3 2027
-- One day more and (i) applies: it stops on 11 March 2027, the pension-age day.
#ASSERT `When does my weekly compensation stop` `10 March 2025` (`on` 11 3 2027) FALSE `any day` EQUALS `on` 11 3 2027
-- Already past pension age at the accident: 104 weeks.
#ASSERT `When does my weekly compensation stop` `10 March 2025` (`on` 1 1 2024) FALSE `any day` EQUALS `on` 8 3 2027
-- Finding 25: s 33 lets the Commission extend "the time limits imposed by this Act on the payment of benefits under Part ... 4" for
-- special hardship. Extended from 8 March 2027 to 30 June 2027: 30 June 2027. An "extension" to an earlier day leaves 8 March 2027.
#ASSERT `When does my weekly compensation stop` `10 March 2025` (`on` 1 1 2024) TRUE (`on` 30 6 2027) EQUALS `on` 30 6 2027
#ASSERT `When does my weekly compensation stop` `10 March 2025` (`on` 1 1 2024) TRUE (`on` 1 1 2027) EQUALS `on` 8 3 2027

§§ `s 14 -- young persons`

-- s 14(2) Table. Born 1 May 2006: 18 on 17 March 2025, 70%; married (s 14(3)), 100%.
#ASSERT `What percentage of weekly compensation do I get at my age` (`on` 1 5 2006) `17 March 2025` FALSE EQUALS 70%
#ASSERT `What percentage of weekly compensation do I get at my age` (`on` 1 5 2006) `17 March 2025` TRUE EQUALS 100%
-- Born 1 May 2004: 20, 90%. Born 17 March 2004: 21 that day, 100%. Born 1 June 2009: 15, 40%.
#ASSERT `What percentage of weekly compensation do I get at my age` (`on` 1 5 2004) `17 March 2025` FALSE EQUALS 90%
#ASSERT `What percentage of weekly compensation do I get at my age` (`on` 17 3 2004) `17 March 2025` FALSE EQUALS 100%
#ASSERT `What percentage of weekly compensation do I get at my age` (`on` 1 6 2009) `17 March 2025` FALSE EQUALS 40%

-- s 14(1). A 12-year-old student (born 15 January 2013) hurt on 10 March 2025, still at school: no start yet.
#ASSERT `From when can I be paid weekly compensation` `10 March 2025` (`on` 15 1 2013) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS `benefits wait until full-time study stops, or marriage or a de facto relationship`
-- Leaves school on 1 December 2030: the later of turning 15 (15 January 2028) and that day.
#ASSERT `From when can I be paid weekly compensation` `10 March 2025` (`on` 15 1 2013) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`on` 1 12 2030) EQUALS `benefits may be paid only from` (`on` 1 12 2030)
-- A 10-year-old not at school (READING: nothing to cease): from the 15th birthday, 15 January 2030.
#ASSERT `From when can I be paid weekly compensation` `10 March 2025` (`on` 15 1 2015) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS `benefits may be paid only from` (`on` 15 1 2030)
-- A 17-year-old student, unmarried, earning little, who leaves school on 30 November 2026.
#ASSERT `From when can I be paid weekly compensation` `10 March 2025` (`on` 1 5 2007) TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE (`on` 30 11 2026) EQUALS `benefits may be paid only from` (`on` 30 11 2026)
-- The same student earning more than 25% of average Territory earnings: s 14(1)(b)(iii) is not met.
#ASSERT `From when can I be paid weekly compensation` `10 March 2025` (`on` 1 5 2007) TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE (`on` 30 11 2026) EQUALS `s 14(1) does not apply`
#ASSERT `From when can I be paid weekly compensation` `10 March 2025` `born 1985` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS `s 14(1) does not apply`
-- Finding 27: born 29 February 2012, 13 at the accident and not at school. 2027 is a common year, so she turns 15 on 1 March 2027
-- (READING), the day `the age of a person born` also makes her 15: payable from 1 March 2027, not 28 February.
#ASSERT `From when can I be paid weekly compensation` `10 March 2025` (`on` 29 2 2012) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `any day` EQUALS `benefits may be paid only from` (`on` 1 3 2027)
#ASSERT `What percentage of weekly compensation do I get at my age` (`on` 29 2 2012) (`on` 1 3 2027) FALSE EQUALS 40%

§§ `s 13 -- the weekly amount`

-- Base: the s 13(3) figure, $1,200, below MA ($1,500).
#ASSERT `weekly` `10 March 2025` `17 March 2025` `born 1985` `pension 2052` 1500 1200 0 0 `any day` `any day` (LIST "reduced", "married or dependant") EQUALS `the weekly benefit, in dollars, is` 1200
-- s 13(2)(a): MA is "the maximum amount payable per week": $1,800 calculated, $1,500 paid.
#ASSERT `weekly` `10 March 2025` `17 March 2025` `born 1985` `pension 2052` 1500 1800 0 0 `any day` `any day` (LIST "reduced") EQUALS `the weekly benefit, in dollars, is` 1500
-- s 11: no seatbelt, 25% off: 1,200 - 300 = 900.
#ASSERT `weekly` `10 March 2025` `17 March 2025` `born 1985` `pension 2052` 1500 1200 0 0 `any day` `any day` (LIST "reduced", "no seatbelt") EQUALS `the weekly benefit, in dollars, is` 900
-- s 11A: $200 a week of income protection insurance: 1,200 - 200 = 1,000.
#ASSERT `weekly` `10 March 2025` `17 March 2025` `born 1985` `pension 2052` 1500 1200 0 200 `any day` `any day` (LIST "reduced") EQUALS `the weekly benefit, in dollars, is` 1000
-- s 11B, both: (1,200 x 75%) - 200 = 700.
#ASSERT `weekly` `10 March 2025` `17 March 2025` `born 1985` `pension 2052` 1500 1200 0 200 `any day` `any day` (LIST "reduced", "no seatbelt") EQUALS `the weekly benefit, in dollars, is` 700
-- s 13(2)(b)(iii): earning $1,500, "equal to or exceeding the maximum amount": nothing; $1,499: the s 13(3) figure.
#ASSERT `weekly` `10 March 2025` `17 March 2025` `born 1985` `pension 2052` 1500 1200 1500 0 `any day` `any day` (LIST "reduced") EQUALS `nothing is payable for that week` `earnings that week were at least the maximum amount (s 13(2)(b)(iii))`
#ASSERT `weekly` `10 March 2025` `17 March 2025` `born 1985` `pension 2052` 1500 1200 1499 0 `any day` `any day` (LIST "reduced") EQUALS `the weekly benefit, in dollars, is` 1200
-- s 13(2)(b)(ii), (5)(b), (5)(c), (1).
#ASSERT `weekly` `10 March 2025` `17 March 2025` `born 1985` `pension 2052` 1500 1200 0 0 `any day` `any day` (LIST "reduced", "full time") EQUALS `nothing is payable for that week` `the Commission determined the person capable of full-time work that week (s 13(2)(b)(ii))`
#ASSERT `weekly` `10 March 2025` `17 March 2025` `born 1985` `pension 2052` 1500 1200 0 0 `any day` `any day` (LIST "reduced", "prison") EQUALS `nothing is payable for that week` `detained in a penal institution (s 13(5)(b))`
#ASSERT `weekly` `10 March 2025` `17 March 2025` `born 1985` `pension 2052` 1500 1200 0 0 `any day` `any day` (LIST "reduced", "outside Australia") EQUALS `nothing is payable for that week` `outside Australia (s 13(5)(c))`
