    PARTY `the claimant` DOES `claim damages or compensation under the law of the place of the accident` AT 10
    PARTY `the claimant` DOES `give the Commission written notice of the claim` AT 11
-- expect: still owed: the claimant MUST reimburse the Commission 20000 (only $15,000 repaid, which does not match)
#TRACE (`s 7(3) -- a claimant who claims in the other jurisdiction must tell the Commission at once, and repay benefits from what is awarded` 20000 50000) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the claimant` DOES `claim damages or compensation under the law of the place of the accident` AT 10
    PARTY `the claimant` DOES `give the Commission written notice of the claim` AT 10
    PARTY `the claimant` DOES `reimburse the Commission` 15000 AT 400

-- s 31: 10 March 2025 to 10 March 2028 is 365 + 365 + 366 = 1,096 days. A claim on day 1,096 is in time.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 31 -- a claim must be made as soon as practicable, and the Commission must refuse one made after the s 31(3) limit` 1096) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `make the claim in the approved form` 1096)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 31 -- a claim must be made as soon as practicable, and the Commission must refuse one made after the s 31(3) limit` 1096) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `make the claim in the approved form` 30)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the claimant, "s 31(3): ..." (claim on day 1,097)
#TRACE (`s 31 -- a claim must be made as soon as practicable, and the Commission must refuse one made after the s 31(3) limit` 1096) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the claimant` DOES `make the claim in the approved form` AT 1097
-- The same rule from the dates (`the days from`): 1,096 days from 10 March 2025 to 10 March 2028, hand-counted above. For the claimant
-- born 29 February 2008 (finding 27), to 1 March 2029: 1,096 days to 10 March 2028, 365 more to 10 March 2029 (no 29 February in
-- between), less 9 days: 1,452.
#ASSERT `the days from` `10 March 2025` `to` (`on` 10 3 2028) EQUALS 1096
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`the s 31 claim rule, from an accident on` `10 March 2025` `for a claimant born` `born 1985`) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `make the claim in the approved form` 1096)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`the s 31 claim rule, from an accident on` `10 March 2025` `for a claimant born` (`on` 29 2 2008)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `make the claim in the approved form` 1452)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the claimant, "s 31(3): ..." (claim on day 1,097 from the dates)
#TRACE (`the s 31 claim rule, from an accident on` `10 March 2025` `for a claimant born` `born 1985`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the claimant` DOES `make the claim in the approved form` AT 1097

-- s 18BD(4) (finding 26): the adult claiming on 1 April 2025 (clock day 0). 1 April 2025 to 1 April 2028 is 365 + 365 + 366 = 1,096
-- days; the Commission's last day, 31 March 2028, is day 1,095. A determination on day 1,095 is in time.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 18BD(4) -- the Commission must decide on long-term attendant care before interim care ceases, for a person born` `born 1985` `injured on` `10 March 2025` `who claimed on` (`on` 1 4 2025)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the Commission` `determine whether the injured person is eligible for long-term attendant care benefits under s 18BC` 1095)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- An injury before 1 July 2014: no s 18BD duty (s 18BA).
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 18BD(4) -- the Commission must decide on long-term attendant care before interim care ceases, for a person born` `born 1985` `injured on` (`on` 1 6 2014) `who claimed on` (`on` 1 4 2015)) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `make the claim in the approved form` 5)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the Commission, "s 18BD(4): ..." (determination on day 1,096, 1 April 2028, the day interim benefits cease)
#TRACE (`s 18BD(4) -- the Commission must decide on long-term attendant care before interim care ceases, for a person born` `born 1985` `injured on` `10 March 2025` `who claimed on` (`on` 1 4 2025)) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commission` DOES `determine whether the injured person is eligible for long-term attendant care benefits under s 18BC` AT 1096

-- s 31A: a passenger owes nothing; a driver who reports within the (illustrative) day the Traffic Regulations allow.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 31A -- a driver must report the accident as the Traffic Regulations require, or the Commission may refuse the claim` FALSE 1) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `make the claim in the approved form` 5)) EQUALS FULFILLED
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`s 31A -- a driver must report the accident as the Traffic Regulations require, or the Commission may refuse the claim` TRUE 1) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `report the accident as reg 19(2) of the Traffic Regulations 1999 requires` 1)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- expect: BREACH BY the claimant, "s 31A: ..." (reported on day 2)
#TRACE (`s 31A -- a driver must report the accident as the Traffic Regulations require, or the Commission may refuse the claim` TRUE 1) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the claimant` DOES `report the accident as reg 19(2) of the Traffic Regulations 1999 requires` AT 2

-- ss 28A, 28B, 28E: notice received at day 0; review asked on day 30; the s 28B deadline 42 days after the request (1 September to
-- 13 October 2025); decision on day 72; referral to the Tribunal on day 100, the 28th day after.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 28A, 28B, 28E -- ask for review within 90 days, a review decision within 30 business days, then the Tribunal within 28 days` 42) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `ask the designated person to review the original decision` 30), (EVENT `the designated person` `make the review decision` 72), (EVENT `the claimant` `refer the matter to the Tribunal` 100)) EQUALS FULFILLED
-- Not asking for a review is no breach.
#ASSERT EVALTRACE (`ss 28A, 28B, 28E -- ask for review within 90 days, a review decision within 30 business days, then the Tribunal within 28 days` 42) 0 (LIST (EVENT `the claimant` `make the claim in the approved form` 120)) EQUALS FULFILLED
